From 1bd3eb76bac9c7f3f31a5c089c1b9623496d498c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 23:40:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] luma: Beam finds files, folders and Settings pages in one
 ranked list

Beam (Luma Search) now shows files and folders from the LocalSearch index
and Settings pages and options, and orders apps, settings, files and
folders in a single list by score instead of one block per provider.

- lumaSearchRanking.js scores names: exact, prefix, word prefix, substring,
  then typos for longer words, accent-, case- and punctuation-insensitive
  ("wifi" is "Wi-Fi"). Standard folders (Documents, Downloads, Pictures,
  Music, Videos, Desktop), recently used files, results picked before and
  shallow places under home rank higher. Backups, copies, dated, hashed and
  versioned names and build, cache and dependency folders rank lower,
  unless those words were typed.
- lumaFileIndex.js asks LocalSearch (tinysparql) for names starting with
  the typed words, shortest names and shortest paths, with prepared
  statements and async cursors, and adds recently-used.xbel, Search picks
  and the top of home. It honours remember-recent-files and
  recent-files-max-age; without LocalSearch, Search works without files.
- lumaFileSearch.js replaces Filer's D-Bus provider inside Beam. It checks
  results still exist, honours the Files switch in Settings -> Search and
  Luma Search's file kind, opens with the default app and shows the item
  in Filer on Ctrl+Enter or the row's folder button.
- lumaSettingsSearch.js reads luma-search's settings-pages.json (pages,
  options and everyday words, e.g. "sleep" -> Power > Automatic Suspend)
  and opens the panel through Settings' launch-panel action. Settings rows
  stay together, one per name, at most four.
- In compact mode apps, files and settings pages search at once and D-Bus
  providers after 90 ms, instead of everything after 150 ms.
